- op: create  # 4c01
  at: '2026-09-17T03:41:05Z'  # 4c01
  by: agent  # 4c01
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4c01
  clock: 1  # 4c01
  nonce: 4c01  # 4c01
  data:  # 4c01
    kind: work_item  # 4c01
    title: "rust-analyzer's 'backend produced no output' is filed as a SKIP but the pass RAN: no skip_reason_code fits it, and its real home is silence_reason=candidates_unresolved"  # 4c01
    status: todo_hard  # 4c01
    priority: 3  # 4c01
    parent:  # 4c01
    tags:  # 4c01
    - analysis_quality  # 4c01
    - disclosure  # 4c01
    isbefore: []  # 4c01
    duplicate_of: []  # 4c01
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 4c01
    pr_ref:  # 4c01
    description: "Found during WI-dukoh's conversion of 49 skip sites to skip_reason_code. Every\nother site classified cleanly; this one has no honest code, and it is filed\nrather than folded into a neighbour.\n\nTHE SITE. hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer/analyzer.py:\n\n    result = try_analyze_with_rust_analyzer(...)\n    if result is None:\n        return AnalysisResult(\n            skipped=True, skip_reason=\"rust-analyzer backend produced no output\",\n        )\n\nWHY NO CODE FITS.\n  backend_disabled       -- FALSE. The backend was enabled; the gate above\n                            already returned for the disabled case.\n  dependency_unavailable -- FALSE. Nothing was missing.\n  pass_crashed           -- FALSE. Nothing raised; try_analyze_with_rust_analyzer\n                            returned None.\n  no_candidate_files     -- FALSE and dangerous. The repo may be full of .rs.\n\nIt currently takes UNREPORTED, which is the correct declared residue for \"the\nproducer did not classify itself\" and is honest. But the producer DID say\nsomething; the axis has no value for what it said.\n\nTHE DEEPER PROBLEM, which is why this is a row and not a one-line fix: THIS IS\nNOT A SKIP. The pass RAN. It invoked the backend, the backend returned nothing,\nand the pass recorded a skip anyway. A pass that ran and produced nothing is\nthe population `AnalysisRun.silence_reason` exists to explain -- and the\ncorrect answer there already exists (`candidates_unresolved`: the pass carried\nits input through a stage and got nothing out). Recording it in skipped_passes\nputs it in the \"did not run\" bucket, where it inflates the skip denominator and\nis invisible to the silence summary.\n\nSo the choice is between two fixes and they need a decision, not a guess:\n  (a) Stop marking it skipped. Return a real AnalysisRun with\n      silence_reason=candidates_unresolved. Correct, and changes the WI-didil\n      \"every analyzer resolves to exactly one of an AR or a skip\" accounting\n      for this pass.\n  (b) Keep it a skip and declare a new axis value for \"an enabled backend\n      produced nothing\". Cheaper; adds a value whose only producer is one site.\n\n(a) is the better shape on the evidence -- the pass ran, so it belongs in the\nran population -- but it touches a completeness invariant and deserves its own\ndecision.\n\nRELATED: ADR-0056 §\"What would change this decision\" item 5 reserves to the\nOWNER the question of whether a pass that did not run should get an AnalysisRun\nat all. This is the mirror image: a pass that DID run and is filed as if it\nhad not.\n\nSIZING: one producer site, one test. The accounting question is the work."  # 4c01
    fields: {}  # 4c01
- op: discuss  # 9de8
  at: '2026-09-17T18:35:57Z'  # 9de8
  by: agent  # 9de8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9de8
  clock: 2  # 9de8
  nonce: 9de8  # 9de8
  message: "The 2026-09-17 fundamental concept audit of the pass-silence host boundary\nfound the mirror image of this row, and the two should be decided together.\n\nThis row: a pass that RAN (rust-analyzer's backend returned None) is filed as a\nSKIP. The audit found that for the 40 grammar-gated analyzers, a pass that\npartly ran BUILDS AN AnalysisRun -- times itself, appends the INV-pitab warning\nto it -- and collect_analyzer_result then discards it, because\nanalysis_runs.append sits only in the else of \"if is_skipped:\". Live repro in\nWI-gidid.\n\nThat matters for the choice this row poses between (a) stop marking it skipped\nand (b) declare a new axis value. It also re-frames ADR-0056 item 5, which this\nrow cites: the owner was asked whether an AnalysisRun should be EMITTED for a\npass that did not run. For the grammar-gated cohort the real question is\nwhether the one already CREATED should be KEPT -- a materially weaker case for\nthe ADR's ABSENT != EMPTY objection, since those passes did begin work.\n\nAlso relevant to the \"inflates the skip denominator\" point here: measured on\ncomponent-model-demo, 130 of 162 passes carry no_candidate_files, 48 via\nsilence_reason and 82 via skip_reason_code, and the host is chosen by\nLANGUAGE_EXTENSIONS membership and analyzer return style rather than by\nanything about the silence (WI-mamiv). So the denominator problem this row\nnames is not specific to rust-analyzer.\n\nNo action taken on this row. Status unchanged."  # 9de8
- op: discuss  # 4ccd
  at: '2026-09-17T19:46:47Z'  # 4ccd
  by: agent  # 4ccd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4ccd
  clock: 3  # 4ccd
  nonce: 4ccd  # 4ccd
  message: "CORRECTION TO THIS ROW'S PREMISE, from the owner asking whether the backend\nalways comes back with nothing. It does not, and that undermines both options\nthis row offers.\n\n1. THE BACKEND IS PRODUCTIVE. Measured 2026-09-17 at 06699b1d91:\nHYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 on ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/aardvark-dns (16 .rs)\nproduced 637 edges with origin=['scip'] -- MORE than tree-sitter rust's 445,\nand the largest single origin in the artifact. So \"backend produced no output\"\nis a failure path, not the normal path.\n\n2. `result is None` DOES NOT MEAN \"RAN AND PRODUCED NOTHING\". It means the\nbackend FAILED. try_analyze_with_rust_analyzer's own docstring:\n\n    \"Every failure mode WI-nohah lists maps to None; only a successful\n     invoke+translate produces a non-None return.\"\n\nand analyzer.py's module docstring says it \"swallows that to an empty\nAnalysisResult so the registry treats 'no SCIP run' identically to 'SCIP run\nproduced nothing'.\" So the single None return CONFLATES two states:\n  - invoke failed (spawn error, OOM, timeout, non-zero exit)\n  - invoke succeeded, translate yielded nothing\n\n3. THEREFORE THIS ROW'S PROPOSED FIX IS WRONG FOR THE DOMINANT SUB-CASE.\ncandidates_unresolved is declared as \"the pass FOUND its construct and carried\nnone of it through resolution\". A subprocess that failed to run found nothing\nand resolved nothing; it did not carry candidates through a stage. Stamping it\ncandidates_unresolved would assert a measurement that never happened -- the\nsame class of error as the no_candidate_files claim this row correctly rejects.\n\n4. AND OPTION (b) IS PROBABLY UNNECESSARY. The row says \"the axis has no value\nfor 'an enabled backend produced nothing'\". For the invoke-failure half there\nalready is one: pass_crashed. ADR-0056's init-failure ruling extended it to a\ncontained constructor exception on the explicit grounds that the value \"says\nnothing about WHO contained the raise\", and that \"install the package\" would be\nthe wrong advice. A contained rust-analyzer subprocess failure is the same\nshape. That leaves at most the translate-yielded-nothing half needing a new\nvalue -- and that half cannot be distinguished until the None conflation in (2)\nis unpicked, so no new value can be declared honestly before that.\n\n5. THE BIGGER DEFECT IS ON THE SUCCESS PATH, NOT THIS ONE. When the backend\nSUCCEEDS it returns AnalysisResult(symbols=..., edges=...) with no run=, so the\npass appears in NEITHER analysis_runs NOR skipped_passes (74 + 84 = 158 passes\non that artifact, rust_analyzer in none), and all 637 scip edges carry an\norigin_run_id matching no AnalysisRun -- 1308 cross_field validation violations.\nRecorded in full on WI-jivim.\n\nRECOMMENDED RE-POINT: re-scope this row to \"unpick the None conflation first\",\nwhich is the precondition for classifying either half honestly, and drop the\ncandidates_unresolved prescription. The accounting question this row raised is\nstill real but is now subordinate to the success-path defect, which is larger,\nalready breaks the same WI-didil contract, and does not need an owner ruling to\nbe recognised as a bug.\n\nNo status or priority change made -- both are the owner's."  # 4ccd
- op: discuss  # f7ec
  at: '2026-09-17T20:06:30Z'  # f7ec
  by: agent  # f7ec
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f7ec
  clock: 4  # f7ec
  nonce: f7ec  # f7ec
  message: "ADDENDUM to the correction above, now that the success path has been traced.\n\nrust_analyzer is the ONLY one of 118 registered analyzers that can be absent\nfrom BOTH analysis_runs and limits.skipped_passes, and on the success path it\nis (74 + 84 = 158 passes on the aardvark-dns artifact; it is in none). So this\nrow's complaint -- \"marking it a SKIP is itself questionable, since the pass\ndid run\" -- has a sharper sibling: on the path where it runs SUCCESSFULLY it is\nnot marked at all.\n\nBoth branches of the same function are wrong in opposite directions:\n\n    result is None      -> filed as a skip           (this row: it ran)\n    result is not None  -> filed as nothing at all   (WI-didag: 1306 orphans)\n\nThat matters for choosing between this row's options (a) and (b). Option (a) --\nreturn a real AnalysisRun instead of a skip -- is the SAME change WI-didag needs\nfor the success path, so doing them together is one coherent fix to one\nfunction rather than two separate rulings. Option (b) -- keep it a skip and add\na ninth vocabulary value -- leaves the success path broken and adds a value\nwhose meaning (\"an enabled backend produced nothing\") cannot be distinguished\nfrom \"the backend failed to run\" until the None conflation is unpicked.\n\nThis strengthens the recommendation already recorded: re-scope to \"unpick the\nNone conflation\", and expect (a) to fall out of WI-didag's threading fix rather\nthan needing a separate accounting ruling. No status or priority change made."  # f7ec
