- op: discuss  # 99d8
  at: '2026-09-17T21:55:54Z'  # 99d8
  by: agent  # 99d8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 99d8
  clock: 6  # 99d8
  nonce: 99d8  # 99d8
  message: "FIXED. Closed on a live repro of both halves this row names.\n\nTHE TWO COMPLAINTS, and what each got:\n\n1. \"no skip_reason_code fits it\" -- because ONE None was hiding FOUR states.\n   The exception taxonomy already distinguished RustAnalyzerNotInstalled /\n   RustAnalyzerInvocationFailed / RustAnalyzerNoOutput / DecodeError, and\n   try_analyze_with_rust_analyzer threw that away at the boundary. It now\n   returns a ScipAttempt carrying the verdict:\n\n     missing binary        -> dependency_unavailable  (\"install it\" IS the advice)\n     non-zero exit/timeout -> pass_crashed            (ADR-0056 init-failure ruling:\n                                                       the value says nothing about\n                                                       WHO contained the raise)\n     undecodable SCIP      -> pass_crashed            (same shape)\n     exit 0, no index      -> unreported              (see below)\n\n   LIVE REPRO, HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 survey of a NON-cargo repo\n   (~/whole_bunch_of_repos/compose-go):\n\n     BEFORE  {\"reason\": \"rust-analyzer backend produced no output\",\n              \"skip_reason_code\": \"unreported\"}\n     AFTER   {\"reason\": \"rust-analyzer backend: rust-analyzer scip exited 1\",\n              \"skip_reason_code\": \"pass_crashed\"}\n\n2. \"marking it a SKIP is itself questionable, since the pass did run.\"\n   Correct, and now fixed for the state that actually describes -- a backend\n   that RAN TO COMPLETION and indexed nothing. That returns a real AnalysisRun\n   with silence_reason=no_candidate_construct, a positive body claim. Falling\n   through to derive_silence_reason would have stamped no_candidate_files\n   (\"received zero input files, and no mechanism would change it\") on a repo\n   that may be full of .rs -- the ADR-0056 W3 false assertion one pass to the\n   left. Proven on the aardvark-dns run under WI-didag: rust_analyzer is in\n   analysis_runs, not skipped_passes.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT DO, AND WHY. This row offered (a) stop marking it skipped or\n(b) declare a ninth axis value. Neither, as posed:\n\n  * (a) is right ONLY for the ran-to-completion state, which is what shipped.\n    For a missing binary or a contained crash the pass genuinely did not\n    produce, and those stay on the skip host -- re-hosting dependency_unavailable\n    and pass_crashed onto an AnalysisRun is precisely the question ADR-0056\n    item 5 reserves to the OWNER. Telling the states apart does not pre-empt it.\n  * (b) is unnecessary for three of the four states, which existing values fit\n    honestly. It remains arguable for the fourth (exit 0, no index written:\n    not a crash, not a missing dependency, and the axis has no value for \"an\n    enabled backend completed without producing anything to read\"). That one\n    keeps the declared residue and the gap is documented in ScipAttempt's\n    docstring rather than filled with a plausible neighbour.\n\nCORRECTION TO THIS ROW'S PREMISE, recorded earlier in this thread and\nconfirmed by the work: \"backend produced no output\" is the FAILURE path, not\nthe normal one. The backend is productive -- 637 edges on aardvack-dns, more\nthan tree-sitter rust's 445. And candidates_unresolved, which this row\nproposed, would have been wrong: a subprocess that failed to run did not carry\ncandidates through a stage.\n\nTESTS: 9 written RED first, all green. 4788 passed; ratchet 667 (delta +0).\nFive pre-existing tests and one assertion on the conflated prose string were\nRE-POINTED, not deleted -- the behaviour they protected still holds."  # 99d8
